WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.772
A research paper starts as one idea,

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.161
and ends up as a hundred loose pieces.

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.411
AutoWriterAI keeps them all on one canvas.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.504
Lay out your manuscript
as connected blocks,

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.131
from the research question
to the cover letter.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.774
Then write in the order
real papers get written:

00:00:17.069 --> 00:00:19.243
methods first, abstract last.

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:23.789
With Tre Lune, highlight a passage
in a source, and keep it as a stitch.

00:00:23.954 --> 00:00:25.763
Weave your stitches into a paragraph,

00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:28.111
and every citation stays attached.

00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:30.897
Pause, and U'lama' reads what you wrote.

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.248
It checks your argument,

00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:34.238
your logic and your consistency,

00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:36.517
and shows you exactly what to fix.

00:00:36.928 --> 00:00:39.875
And it runs on your own
computer, even the AI.

00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:41.825
Your draft never leaves the room.

00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:43.361
AutoWriterAI.

00:00:43.401 --> 00:00:45.891
From first idea to published paper.

00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:47.072
Coming soon.
